C. THE LOW-Z ANCHOR -- *** THE MISSED REFRAMING. OPEN, and it is the right size. ***
====================================================================================================
  Mechanism: the Hubble-diagram intercept is pinned by low-z SNe (z ~ 0.02-0.08). A coherent
  local flow adds dv to their redshifts, biasing mu(z) exactly at the low-z end -- and the
  literature ALREADY claims 'the DESI hint for dynamical DE is biased by low-z supernovae'
  (surfaced in the 2026-07-30 search, independent of any modified inertia).
  The framework's OWN standing (mi_bulkflow_and_initial_conditions_2026): the environmental
  reading boosts linear flows by nu ~ 1.2-1.7 over LCDM. LCDM sigma_v at the relevant depth
  is ~250 km/s, so MI adds a COHERENT ~50-175 km/s the standard analysis does not model.
  Size of the resulting distance-modulus bias, dmu = (5/ln10)(dv/c)/z:
        z       dv=50      dv=100      dv=175
    0.020      0.0181      0.0362      0.0634
    0.035      0.0103      0.0207      0.0362
    0.050      0.0072      0.0145      0.0254
    0.080      0.0045      0.0091      0.0158
  (mag; compare the phantom signal 0.025-0.069 mag)
  [OK] the MI flow-boost per-SN bias spans 0.005-0.063 mag -- SAME ORDER as the 0.025-0.069 mag phantom signal and overlapping its band (not bracketing it; and sky-averaging dilutes it further). Right order, genuinely missed
  WHY THIS IS NOT ALREADY THE CLOSED BULK-FLOW DOOR: mi_bulkflow_sigma8_consistency_2026
  closed the question 'can any theory produce the claimed 1.9x flow EXCESS' (no -- sigma8/
  RSD/BAO forbid it). THIS channel needs no excess: the framework's own MODEST nu ~ 1.2-1.7
  boost, applied to ordinary flows, biases the SN anchor without touching sigma8 at the
  forbidden level. Different question, not closed by that no-go.
  WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED (both matter):
   * the SIGN -- whether the bias mimics phantom (w0>-1, wa<0) or anti-phantom requires the
     actual monopole/dipole of the local flow field and the actual fit, not this estimate;
   * NOVELTY IS THIN -- 'low-z SNe bias the DESI hint' is already published without MI, and
     the local-void/timescape literature owns the mundane version. The framework's only
     addition is the 1.2-1.7x amplification and its a0-tied environment dependence.
  [OK] channel C: OPEN -- right size, sign undetermined, novelty honestly thin

